nner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ \n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413393 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c2afbe9-632c-56a2-8877-4a2cf3a61d97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413393 #edb/ref 1074 "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-7\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(-1-(-1))+\\frac{1}{6}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186450518 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450518 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450518 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4a08bf6-bbd5-5c7a-a458-cc2f28795f81" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450519 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450519 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450519 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bc472246-cf39-501b-88ba-aea193a2227d" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450520 #edb/ref 1080 "f